horylation", "stId": "R-SSC-8853419", "stIdVersion": "R-SSC-8853419.1", "isInDisease": false, "isInferred": true, "maxDepth": 1, "name": ["TPX2 promotes AURKA autophosphorylation"], "releaseDate": "2026-03-25", "speciesName": "Sus scrofa", "inferredFrom": [8853419], "species": [{"dbId": 49633, "displayName": "Sus scrofa", "name": ["Sus scrofa", "pig", "swine"], "taxId": "9823", "abbreviation": "SSC", "className": "Species", "schemaClass": "Species"}], "category": "transition", "className": "Reaction", "schemaClass": "Reaction"}, {"dbId": 10307564, "displayName": "TPX2 promotes AURKA autophosphorylation", "stId": "R-CFA-8853419", "stIdVersion": "R-CFA-8853419.1", "isInDisease": false, "isInferred": true, "maxDepth": 1, "name": ["TPX2 promotes AURKA autophosphorylation"], "releaseDate": "2026-03-25", "speciesName": "Canis familiaris", "inferredFrom": [8853419], "species": [{"dbId": 49646, "displayName": "Canis familiaris", "name": ["Canis familiaris", "Canis lupus familiaris"], "taxId": "9615", "abbreviation": "CFA", "className": "Species", "schemaClass": "Species"}], "category": "transition", "className": "Reaction", "schemaClass": "Reaction"}, {"dbId": 10198915, "displayName": "TPX2 promotes AURKA autophosphorylation", "stId": "R-RNO-8853419", "stIdVersion": "R-RNO-8853419.1", "isInDisease": false, "isInferred": true, "maxDepth": 1, "name": ["TPX2 promotes AURKA autophosphorylation"], "releaseDate": "2026-03-25", "speciesName": "Rattus norvegicus", "inferredFrom": [8853419], "species": [{"dbId": 48895, "displayName": "Rattus norvegicus", "name": ["Rattus norvegicus", "R. norvegicus", "Rn", "brown rat", "Norway rat"], "taxId": "10116", "abbreviation": "RNO", "className": "Species", "schemaClass": "Species"}], "category": "transition", "className": "Reaction", "schemaClass": "Reaction"}, {"dbId": 10076286, "displayName": "TPX2 promotes AURKA autophosphorylation", "stId": "R-MMU-8853419", "stIdVersion": "R-MMU-8853419.1", "isInDisease": false, "isInferred": true, "maxDepth": 1, "name": ["TPX2 promotes AURKA autophosphorylation"], "releaseDate": "2026-03-25", "speciesName": "Mus musculus", "inferredFrom": [8853419], "species": [{"dbId": 48892, "displayName": "Mus musculus", "name": ["Mus musculus", "M. musculus", "Mm", "house mouse"], "taxId": "10090", "abbreviation": "MMU", "className": "Species", "schemaClass": "Species"}], "category": "transition", "className": "Reaction", "schemaClass": "Reaction"}], "reviewed": [{"dbId": 8857944, "displayName": "Maxwell, Christopher A, 2016-02-16", "dateTime": "2016-02-16 05:00:00", "className": "InstanceEdit", "schemaClass": "InstanceEdit"}, {"dbId": 8857945, "displayName": "Chen, Helen, 2016-02-16", "dateTime": "2016-02-16 05:00:00", "className": "InstanceEdit", "schemaClass": "InstanceEdit"}], "species": [48887], "summation": [{"dbId": 8853421, "displayName": "TPX2 promotes aurora kinase A (AURKA) activation via autopho...", "text": "TPX2 promotes aurora kinase A (AURKA) activation via autophosphorylation of AURKA on threonine residue T288. Continuous association of TPX2 with AURKA facilitates active state conformation of AURKA and may prevent inactivation of AURKA by protein phosphatases (Bayliss et al. 2003).<p>Molecular dynamic simulations suggest the existence of two TPX2-dependent switches for Aurora A activation. 1) TPX2 binding to Aurora A forces lysine residue K143 of AURKA into an \u201copen\u201d state, which pulls ADP out of the ATP binding site in AURKA to promote kinase activation. 2) Arginine residue R180 of AURKA undergoes a \u201cclosed\u201d movement upon TPX2 binding, thus capturing phosphorylated threonine T288 of AURKA into a buried position and locking AURKA in its active conformation. The existence of two TPX2-dependent switches in AURKA activation was further verified by the analysis of two AURKA mutants (K143A and R180A) (Xu et al. 2011).AURKA activation is enabled through phosphorylation and TPX2 binding; these two activating switches act synergistically and withough a predefined order (Dodson and Bayliss 2012).", "className": "Summation", "schemaClass": "Summation"}], "reviewStatus": {"dbId": 9821382, "displayName": "five stars", "definition": "externally reviewed", "name": ["five stars"], "className": "ReviewStatus", "schemaClass": "ReviewStatus"}, "isChimeric": false, "category": "transition", "catalystActivity": [{"dbId": 8853423, "displayName": "protein serine/threonine kinase activity of Centrosome:AURKA:TPX2:HMMR [cytosol]", "catalyzedEvent": [8853419], "physicalEntity": {"dbId": 8853414, "displayName": "Centrosome:AURKA:TPX2:HMMR [cytosol]", "stId": "R-HSA-8853414", "stIdVersion": "R-HSA-8853414.1", "maxDepth": 5, "name": ["Centrosome:AURKA:TPX2:HMMR"], "speciesName": "Homo sapiens", "catalystActivities": [8853423], "literatureReference": [8853412], "consumedByEvent": [8853419], "isChimeric": false, "species": [48887], "inDisease": false, "schemaClass": "Complex", "className": "Complex"}, "className": "CatalystActivity", "schemaClass": "CatalystActivity"}], "input": [{"dbId": 113592, "displayName": "ATP [cytosol]", "stId": "R-ALL-113592", "stIdVersion": "R-ALL-113592.5", "maxDepth": 1, "name": ["ATP", "Adenosine 5'-triphosphate", "ATP(4-)"], "crossReference": [{"dbId": 29359, "displayName": "COMPOUND:C00002", "databaseName": "COMPOUND", "identifier": "C00002", "url": "https://www.kegg.jp/entry/C00002", "className": "DatabaseIdentifier", "schemaClass": "DatabaseIdentifier"}], "isRequired": [{"dbId": 72781, "displayName": "Requirement by 'ATP [cytosol]'", "stId": "R-HSA-72781", "stIdVersion": "R-HSA-72781.1", "regulator": 113592, "schemaClass": "Requirement", "className": "Requirement"}], "negativelyRegulates": [{"dbId": 453366, "displayName": "Negative regulation by 'ATP [cytosol]'", "stId": "R-HSA-453366", "stIdVersion": "R-HSA-453366.1", "regulator": 113592, "schemaClass": "NegativeRegulation", "className": "NegativeRegulation"}, {"dbId": 1306812, "displayName": "Negative regulation by 'ATP [cytosol]'", "stId": "R-HS